    <string name="pp_overview">Overview</string>
    <string name="pp_overview_1">Learn Morse (\"the app\") teaches Morse code. It has no accounts and we don\'t collect your name, email, contacts or other information that identifies you directly. This policy explains what data the app and the Google services it uses handle.</string>
    <string name="pp_device">Data stored on your device</string>
    <string name="pp_device_1">Your lesson progress, stars, unlocked lessons, sound settings and Premium status are saved only on your device. They are never sent to us.</string>
    <string name="pp_device_2">Text you type in the translator is converted on your device and is not saved or sent anywhere.</string>
    <string name="pp_device_3">If Android backup is turned on, Android may include this data in your device backup to your Google account. You can manage this in your device\'s backup settings.</string>
    <string name="pp_ads">Advertising</string>
    <string name="pp_ads_1">The free version shows ads from Google AdMob. To show and measure ads, and to prevent fraud, Google may collect your device\'s advertising ID, IP address, approximate location based on that IP address, device and app information, and how you interact with ads. See how Google uses this data.</string>
    <string name="pp_ads_1_link">how Google uses this data</string>
    <string name="pp_ads_2">In the EEA, UK and other regions where the law requires it, the app asks for your consent before personalized ads are shown. You can change your choice at any time in Settings under Ad privacy options.</string>
    <string name="pp_ads_3">You can also reset or delete your advertising ID in your device\'s Android settings. Buying Premium removes all ads.</string>
    <string name="pp_analytics">Analytics and crash reports</string>
    <string name="pp_analytics_1">The app uses Google Firebase Analytics to understand how it is used, for example which screens and lessons are opened, how long sessions last and whether Premium is bought. Firebase may collect an app instance ID, the advertising ID, device model, operating system and app version, language, and approximate location such as your country.</string>
    <string name="pp_analytics_2">The app uses Google Firebase Crashlytics to find and fix crashes. When the app crashes, Crashlytics sends a crash report with the error details, device model, operating system and app version, and a Crashlytics installation ID.</string>
    <string name="pp_analytics_3">This data doesn\'t include your name or email, and we use it only to improve the app. See Firebase privacy and security.</string>
    <string name="pp_analytics_3_link">Firebase privacy and security</string>
    <string name="pp_purchases">Purchases</string>
    <string name="pp_purchases_1">Premium is bought through Google Play. Google processes the payment; we never see your card or payment details. The app only receives confirmation that Premium was purchased, to unlock it. See the Google Play privacy policy.</string>
    <string name="pp_purchases_1_link">Google Play privacy policy</string>
    <string name="pp_ratings">Ratings</string>
    <string name="pp_ratings_1">The app may ask you to rate it using Google Play\'s in-app review. Your rating and review are sent to Google Play, not to us.</string>
    <string name="pp_children">Children</string>
    <string name="pp_children_1">The app is not directed at children under 13, and we don\'t knowingly collect personal information from children.</string>
    <string name="pp_delete">Deleting your data</string>
    <string name="pp_delete_1">To delete everything the app has stored on your device, clear the app\'s data in your device\'s settings or uninstall the app.</string>
    <string name="pp_delete_2">Analytics and crash data are kept by Google Firebase for a limited time and then deleted automatically. To ask for this data to be deleted sooner, email us at %1$s.</string>
    <string name="pp_changes">Changes to this policy</string>
    <string name="pp_changes_1">We may update this policy. Changes take effect when published, and the date at the top shows when it was last updated.</string>
    <string name="pp_contact">Contact</string>
    <string name="pp_contact_1">If you have questions about this policy, email us at %1$s.</string>
    <string name="pp_reminders_1">If you turn on the daily reminder, the app schedules it on your device. Nothing about it is sent to us.</string>
